! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F211 "STORE LOW ORDER
! TEST ROUTINE", sections B "TEST UNCHANGED REGISTERS" and C
! "INDICATOR TEST" (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.114, octal
! 016245.00-016262.40, the routine's own exit "BD,$+1.0"). Twenty
! rows, and they close F211 out.
!
! B1 is the SLO analogue of F210B: set the accumulator's left half,
! right half and sign byte all to ones, run one SLO(U), then ask three
! separate questions -- L0-63, R0-63 and SB0-7 -- that none of them
! moved. p.97 says "the entire accumulator and sign byte register
! remain unchanged throughout the operation unless used as the
! effective address", and as with SRD the model satisfies it only by
! not writing them.
!
! Note what F211B does NOT have: a zero-pattern sub-test. F210B ran
! both B1 (zeros) and B2 (ones); F211B has only the ones. That is the
! stronger of the two anyway -- an all-ones accumulator is flagged, so
! the flagged path runs, and the sign byte has its sign and all three
! flag bits set -- and F210B's own probing showed the zero half never
! fires, since a zero write leaves zeros zero.
!
! C IS THE INTERESTING OMISSION. It clears MOP with BMOPZ, runs one
! SLO(U), and asks with BZMOP that it came on -- and that is the WHOLE
! indicator test. There is no LC question anywhere in F211, where
! F210D2 had one for SRD. That matches the manual exactly: p.97 lists
! SLO's indicators as MOP, the arithmetic result four, the exponent
! range four and ZM, with no LOST CARRY, because a shift has no carry
! to lose. The model was written that way from the page; F211C is the
! listing agreeing by omission.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! FSLO2 is the listing's own label at its real address, 016245.00 --
! the routine's exit branches back to it.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.176. PASS sits at 016262.40, on the routine's exit; the four
! rows after it (BD,$+1.0 / B,FSLO2 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW) are the
! SSIP return and are not transcribed.
!
! Instructions: C1111, CM1111, SLO(U), CT1010, CT1100, SIC, BRGZ, B,
! BMOPZ, BZMOP, DL(U), C0011.
! verify_fp_arith_f211bc_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)022006.0
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)022052.0
FPK37   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525240

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16245.0
FSLO2   C1111(BU,64), FPK1, 64                 ! F211B1: 1 s remain 1 s
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1
        CM1111(BU,8), 10.0
        SLO(U), ROS
        CT1010(BU,64), FPK1, 64                ! does L0-63 remain + 1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1010(BU,64), FPK1                    ! does R0-63 remain + 1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1100(BU,8), 10.0                     ! does the SB remain + 1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32                               ! F211C: MOP indicator, off to on condition
        BMOPZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK37
        C0011(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20
        SLO(U), ROS
        SIC, SEN
        BZMOP, SERS                            ! error if MOP indicator off
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016262.40: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, FSLO2
